<http://data.silknow.org/object/4ed19765-7415-357c-9481-a6a3261735fa>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Border fragment of embroidered cotton canvas with silk and metal threads, Iran, 1800-1899."@en , "Border fragment of embroidered cotton with couched metal thread and coloured silk in satin stitch, and embroidered through a cotton canvas backing to which glue or size has been applied to secure the threads.\n\nRemains of black silk and silver-gilt threads down the left hand side indicates that this was part of a border.\nIt is not possible to see the ground fabric but threads down the right hand side suggest it might be indigo-dyed plain weave cotton.\nIncomplete design; in the upper part is a rigid green and red vertical stem with two pairs of leaves and one stylised pointed petalled flower with a dark blue, blue and red heart-shaped centre. There are small leaves or buds in green, dark blue and red.  In the lower part is a large silver trefoil which is the top of another motif.\nEmbroidery thread: 2Z silk: dark blue, blue, green, white, light brown and dark green; 2S red silk.\n\nMetal thread:\nSilver strip close S-wound on white silk and silver strip close S-wound on yellow silk.\nCouching worked with dark red silk."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b04f1e61-13b1-3187-943d-455567d9fdce> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Border fragment of embroidered cotton canvas with silk and metal threads, Iran, 1800-1899."@en , "Border fragment of embroidered cotton with couched metal thread and coloured silk in satin stitch, and embroidered through a cotton canvas backing to which glue or size has been applied to secure the threads.\n\nRemains of black silk and silver-gilt threads down the left hand side indicates that this was part of a border.\nIt is not possible to see the ground fabric but threads down the right hand side suggest it might be indigo-dyed plain weave cotton.\nIncomplete design; in the upper part is a rigid green and red vertical stem with two pairs of leaves and one stylised pointed petalled flower with a dark blue, blue and red heart-shaped centre. There are small leaves or buds in green, dark blue and red.  In the lower part is a large silver trefoil which is the top of another motif.\nEmbroidery thread: 2Z silk: dark blue, blue, green, white, light brown and dark green; 2S red silk.\n\nMetal thread:\nSilver strip close S-wound on white silk and silver strip close S-wound on yellow silk.\nCouching worked with dark red silk."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/4ed19765-7415-357c-9481-a6a3261735fa/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/4ed19765-7415-357c-9481-a6a3261735fa/dimension/2> ;
